# Ford Zephyr Mk III four-door saloon, 1962-1966.
#
# The Mk III Zephyr: the flat waist line, the thin roof and the two
# headlamps in a split vertical-bar grille. The Zodiac Mk III of the same
# range has four headlamps and a horizontal-bar grille.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Zephyr
#
# Dimensions 4.591 x 1.759 x 1.454 m, wheelbase 2.718 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level side elevation of a 1964 Zephyr 6
# Mk III; the front and rear three-quarters show the grille, lamps and tail.
#
# Colours: grade (d) for a full model-specific list; grade (c) for
# Ambassador Blue only, recorded on a surviving Zodiac Mk III. Ambassador
# Blue, Ermine White, Goodwood Green and Monaco Red are used. Weights 18, 16,
# 14, 12, total 60, provisional.
#
# Speed 150 km/h. Comfort 62/423, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 62. Classes 1,2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 1962 intro, retires staggered 1982-1985.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/ford-zephyr-mk3.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/ford-zephyr-mk3.dae. References:
# citycars/references/ford-zephyr-mk3/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the grille corners are too square, and the rear fins and
# bumper wrap are simplified. At 128 px the flat waist, thin roof, two-lamp
# vertical-bar grille and finned tail read as a Zephyr Mk III.


obj=citycar
name=FordZephyrMk3(AmbassadorBlue)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=18
intro_year=1962
intro_month=4
retire_year=1985
retire_month=6
speed=150
length=3
class=1,2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=62
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=423

